# EdWebConsole — always apply (pointers only)

**Read order:** `ACTIVE_PROGRAM.md` → `AGENTS.md` (start with § **World-class / institutional code gate** — always on, no activation phrase; ML/ablation work also § **ZERO-BIAS** + § **Ablation contract**) → `CLAUDE.md` (Schwab market-field work).

**Conflicts:** ACTIVE_PROGRAM names the epic; **AGENTS.md is the single source for agent behavior** (banned tools, banned phrases, no permission asks, fix-as-we-find, closure definition + no-deferral, no new files); CLAUDE.md owns Schwab market-field law; project rules beat user rules; MCP tools are tool-scoped; Cursor Skills are task-scoped (follow when invoked, do not override AGENTS).

**Binding scope:** do not treat `governance/*.md` or `docs/plans/*.md` as binding unless ACTIVE_PROGRAM or AGENTS points there for the current epic.

**Workspace:** if not in EdWebConsole, call `move_agent_to_root` before project edits.

**Do not duplicate AGENTS rules here.** This file is a pointer surface only. Add behavior rules to AGENTS.md; mechanical enforcement to `tools/check_*.py` + the matching test file + `.pre-commit-config.yaml`.

**Enforcement (binding — rules are not memos):** Every commit runs `tools/check_fix_everything_we_touch.py` via pre-commit (all `_REPO_WIDE_STATIC_CHECK_FUNCS` locks). Before sign-off: `python tools/enforce_all_rules.py --enforce-all` (exit 0). Claude Code Stop hook runs the same static audit. **Honest limit:** Cursor chat has no Stop hook; violations block at commit time.
